   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "General rule for choosing the auxiliary",
     "texto": [
      "The vast majority of transitive verbs (those that take a direct object: mangiare, leggere, comprare, fare, ascoltare) and many intransitive verbs of activity (parlare, telefonare, camminare, lavorare) use **avere**. The past participle with avere ends neutrally in **-o**: **Ho telefonato a mia madre**.",
      "Verbs of directed movement (andare, venire, partire, arrivare, tornare, uscire, entrare), change of state (nascere, morire, diventare), staying (stare, rimanere) and reflexive verbs use **essere** with compulsory agreement: **Sono arrivata a Roma**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Comparing auxiliaries",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "With «avere» (no agreement)",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "With «essere» (with agreement)",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      }
     ],
